course: dictionary
lesson: 12122
title: Combined
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Combined means put together into one thing or one total. «Their combined score» means all their scores added together.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. If Mia scores 8 and Jo scores 9, the combined score is 17, because you add the two scores together.
explain: To combine means to join or mix two or more things. In cooking, you combine flour, eggs and milk to make a cake. In science, two substances can combine to make something new.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Their added-together score» still makes sense, so combined means added together here.
fact: Combined means put together into one.
fact: To combine means to join or mix two or more things together.
fact: «Their combined score» means their scores added together.
fact: «Combine the ingredients» means mix them all together in one bowl.
fact: A combination is a mix of different things, such as «a combination of sun and rain» that makes a rainbow.
exercise: «Ali scored 4 goals and Ben scored 6. Their combined score was 10.» What does combined mean here? | *Added together | Taken away | Shared out equally | Written down in a list
exercise: Mum says, «Combine the flour, the sugar and the eggs.» What should you do? | *Mix them together | Keep each one in a separate bowl | Eat them one at a time | Throw them all away
exercise: Which word means to join or mix two things together? | Measure | Divide | *Combine | Separate
test: A teacher says, «Combine your answers into one list.» What does combine mean? | Cut apart | Forget | Count backwards | *Join together
test: «Rain combined with wind made the walk hard.» What does combined with mean here? | After | Taken away from | Before | *Added to, along with
exam: «Mia has 8 stickers and Jo has 9. Their combined total is...» What is their combined total? | 1 | 3 | 72 | *17
